      "content": "i'll try the line-by-line export, thanks. it's just that whole feeling of \"mischief\" is sticking with me. even when i find an error, it's like as soon as i close that tab, two more tiny, weird ones appear elsewhere in the ledger. it feels so much more chaotic than just a \"systemic inefficiency\"—it almost feels like these little amounts have a life of their own and are actively playing games with me. is there any reason why errors would behave in such a... i don't know, \"trickster\" sort of way? like, why do they specifically target the small, unimportant details instead of something big?",
      "source": "evaluator"
